# Chart PNGs written by scripts/build_asia_backtest_charts.py under each run
# directory's charts/ subfolder are regenerable from the run's own parquet
# artifacts and are not covered by the parquet/json re-includes above (they
# are two levels deep, e.g. runs/<run_id>/charts/<view>/<slug>.png). Keep
# them out of git history for the same reason the .csv twins are excluded --
# see the run-directory retention note in
# docs/asia-markets/unified-kpi-backtest-v1.md.
data/registries/runs/*/charts/

# Repo-size control: never commit normalized CSVs — the dashboard loader reads the
# parquet twin first (dashboard/data.py load_dataset), so committing the CSV too just
# bloats git history (these are regenerated daily). Keep parquet only. This also
# applies to the top-level asia_backtest_long_form/metrics/metric_intervals CSVs
# above: each has a smaller parquet twin that the engine's own build scripts
# already prefer (see scripts/build_asia_backtest_metrics.py), so only the
# .parquet is committed; the .csv is still written to disk for local inspection,
# just not tracked. asia_backtest_row_status.csv/target_registry.csv/
# document_registry.csv have no parquet twin and stay committed as CSV. Run
# snapshots under data/registries/runs/ follow the same rule: only the .parquet
# twin and the .json manifests/reconciliation are tracked, never the .csv (see
# scripts/prune_backtest_runs.py for how old run directories are retired).
data/normalized/**/*.csv

# Commercial aerospace append-only history used to turn CelesTrak snapshots
# into a real time series across scheduled artifact builds.
!data/normalized/hk_commercial_aerospace/
!data/normalized/hk_commercial_aerospace/*.jsonl

